In order to reduce the chances of a solution deployment being stuck due to permission propagation delays in the platform;
- Added explicit dependencies to creating a BigQuery Data Transfer job config
- Modified the BigQuery Data Transfer Service job configuration so that it runs "every 15 minutes" (the minimum frequency allowed). This makes the job run as soon as possible after the first failed run due to the permission propagation delays.

When publishing an event that results in a duplicate key error, the postgres store currently fails with
> ERROR: current transaction is aborted, commands ignored until end of transaction block (SQLSTATE 25P02)

This results in endlessly looping on attempt to re-insert it in the crdt/replica. 

```
2023-03-13T11:43:30.007-0400	DEBUG	api	api request	{"grpc_service": "xmtp.message_api.v1.MessageApi", "grpc_method": "Publish", "api_client": "", "api_client_version": "", "api_app": "", "api_app_version": "", "client_ip": "127.0.0.1"}
2023-03-13T11:43:30.007-0400	DEBUG	pgstore	inserting head	{"topic": "topic", "event": "4D96DB26…AF9D151E"}
2023-03-13T11:43:30.008-0400	DEBUG	pgstore	ignoring duplicate key error	{"topic": "topic", "error": "ERROR: duplicate key value violates unique constraint \"events_pkey\" (SQLSTATE 23505)", "event": "4D96DB26…AF9D151E"}
2023-03-13T11:43:30.009-0400	ERROR	receiveEventLoop	error inserting head	{"event": "4D96DB26…AF9D151E", "error": "ERROR: current transaction is aborted, commands ignored until end of transaction block (SQLSTATE 25P02)"}
2023-03-13T11:43:30.009-0400	DEBUG	pgstore	inserting head	{"topic": "topic", "event": "4D96DB26…AF9D151E"}
2023-03-13T11:43:30.010-0400	DEBUG	pgstore	ignoring duplicate key error	{"topic": "topic", "error": "ERROR: duplicate key value violates unique constraint \"events_pkey\" (SQLSTATE 23505)", "event": "4D96DB26…AF9D151E"}
2023-03-13T11:43:30.011-0400	ERROR	receiveEventLoop	error inserting head	{"event": "4D96DB26…AF9D151E", "error": "ERROR: current transaction is aborted, commands ignored until end of transaction block (SQLSTATE 25P02)"}
...
```

This PR updates the store to try and avoid the duplicate key error by checking for existence before inserting. 

This may also be surfacing an issue with the crdt/replica logic, but I didn't want to get too deep in there for the work I'm focused on atm and hopefully leave that to the syncer work that ties it all together, or at least for a separate PR that can focus on that.

