This PR adds location data to the `--json` output flag. There is a new location string in the JSON root which describes the filepath of the root Taskfile (entrypoint) and there is a new location object on each task which describes filepath of the Taskfile containing the task and the line/column that the task is defined on.

Since Taskfiles can include other Taskfiles, the location of a task can differ from location of the root taskfile.

Example:

```jsonc
{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "name": "clean",
      "desc": "Cleans temp files and folders",
      "summary": "",
      "up_to_date": false,
      "location": {
        "line": 54,
        "column": 3,
        "taskfile": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml"
      }
    },
    // ...
  ],
  "location": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml"
}
```
